==English==
[[Image:Lapis lazuli block.jpg|thumb|alt=A large stone block|Lapis lazuli (1)]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|lapis lazuli}}, from {{der|en|ML.|-}} {{compound|la|lapis|t1=stone|lazulī|nocat=1}}, genitive singular of {{m|la|lazulum||lapis lazuli, azure, the sky}}, from {{der|en|ar|لَازُوَرْد||lapis lazuli, azure}}, from {{der|en|fa|لاجورد|tr=lâjvard}}. Compare {{m|en|azure}}, of the same origin.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˌlap.ɪs ˈlaz.jʊ.laɪ/|/ˈlaz.jʊ.li/|nocount=1}}
* {{a|GA}} {{enPR|lăp'ĭs lăzʹ(y)ə-lē, lăzʹ(y)ə-lī, lăzhʹə-lē, lăzhʹə-lī}}, {{IPA|en|/ˌlæp.ɪs ˈlæz.(j)ə.li/|/ˈlæz.(j)ə.laɪ/|/ˈlæʒ.ə.li/|/ˈlæʒ.ə.laɪ/|/ləˈzu.li/|nocount=1}}
* {{hyph|en|la|pis la|zu|li}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|lapides lazuli|s}}

# {{lb|en|mineral}} A deep-blue stone, used in making jewelry, and traditionally used to make the pigment [[ultramarine]].
#: {{syn|en|lapis|lazuli|lazurite}}
# {{lb|en|color}} A deep, bright [[blue]], like that of the stone.
#: {{color panel|1B3AB7}}

